   "steps": [
    {
     "math": "12 / 3 = 4.0",
     "text": "Dividing comes before subtracting, so start with `12 / 3`. The slash always gives a decimal answer, even when the numbers divide evenly. So you get `4.0`, not `4`."
    },
    {
     "math": "4.0 - 6 = -2.0",
     "text": "Now subtract 6 from that. Since 6 is bigger than 4.0, the answer goes below zero."
    }
   ],
   "title": "Divide, then subtract",
   "result": "Python gives back `-2.0`. The `.0` stays because the division already made a decimal number.",
   "problem": "What number does Python give back for `12 / 3 - 6`?"
  },
  "kind": "workedExample"
 },
 {
  "screen": 8,
  "content": {
   "basis": {
    "quote": "The slash `/` divides, and Python keeps the part after the decimal point.",
    "position": 5
   },
   "context": "Python runs this line: `15 / 2 - 8`",
   "options": [
    {
     "id": "a",
     "text": "-1",
     "reason": "You cut off the part after the decimal point. Python's `/` keeps it, so 15 / 2 has a .5 at the end.",
     "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
     "id": "b",
     "text": "-0.5",
     "reason": "Python divides 15 by 2 first and keeps the decimal part. Then it subtracts 8, which gives -0.5.",
     "isCorrect": true
