    {
     "id": "c",
     "text": "0.5",
     "reason": "You took the division result away from 8. The line subtracts 8 from the division result, so the answer lands below zero.",
     "isCorrect": false
    }
   ],
   "question": "What number does Python give back?"
  },
  "kind": "check"
 },
 {
  "screen": 9,
  "content": {
   "text": "`18 / 3 * 2` mixes dividing and multiplying. Dividing and multiplying rank the same, so Python works from left to right. `18 / 3` gives `6.0`, then `6.0 * 2` gives `12.0`. Adding and subtracting work the same way.",
   "title": "Same rank, left to right"
  },
  "kind": "explanation"
 },
 {
  "screen": 10,
  "content": {
   "text": "`5 + 2 * 6` gives `17`. To add first, wrap that part in parentheses: `(5 + 2) * 6`. Python always works out what's inside the parentheses first. So it becomes `7 * 6`, which gives `42`.",
   "title": "Parentheses go first"
  },
  "kind": "explanation"
 },
 {
  "screen": 11,
